## Why

The /admin/users page only wired up Make Admin / Demote and Delete. Delete returned 404 because the POST handler used `redirect(...)`, which dropped the rotated admin cookies the api sets on every mutation; the next request hit the unauthed fallback and routed to /login. Same root cause was lurking on Make Admin (worked by luck when no cookie rotation happened). Backend already exposes more user actions (suspend, admin reset-password, lifetime grant, single-user fetch) that had no SSR surface.

## What

- New row actions on /admin/users: View, Reset Password, Lifetime (hidden when already granted), Suspend. Existing Make/Demote Admin and Delete stay.
- New /admin/users/{id} detail page (GET) with a Profile card + an Actions card containing every admin action, so admins can read full context before acting.
- New POST handlers behind admin_guard: user_suspend, user_reset_password, user_grant_lifetime, user_detail (GET). All call the matching bunyip-api endpoint.
- Fix: user_role and user_delete (and every new handler) now use redirect_cookies("/admin/users", &c.set_cookies) instead of redirect(...), so any cookies the api rotates survive the form-submit hop. This is the actual cause of the reported 404s.
- New api/admin.rs client methods: get_user, suspend_user, admin_reset_password, grant_lifetime.

## Notes

- Suspend is one-way today: the api rejects PUT /status with active=true. Reactivation needs its own endpoint, tracked as follow-up.
- Impersonate is intentionally NOT exposed: api endpoint exists but bearer-swap needs its own design pass.

## Test plan

- [ ] /admin/users renders the new buttons.
- [ ] Make Admin / Demote round-trips and stays logged in.
- [ ] Delete actually deletes (no longer 404) and stays logged in.
- [ ] Suspend marks the user inactive.
- [ ] Reset Password triggers the email.
- [ ] Lifetime grant works once and the button hides on the next render.
- [ ] /admin/users/{id} renders for a real user and 404s cleanly for a bad id.
